UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T103612Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movida-labs-dance-technology-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T103612Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: MOVIDA: Labs on Dance and Technology 2026/27
DESCRIPTION:MOVIDA is a Creative Europe co-funded consortium pairing academ
 ic institutions with dance centres across four European cities. Sixteen du
 os\, each made up of one dancer and one creative technologist\, are select
 ed across four themed labs: AI and accessibility in Bucharest\, AI and AR/
 VR in Dusseldorf\, AI and robotics in Lisbon\, and AI and mental health in
  Tallinn. Applicants are assessed on demonstrated capability in integratin
 g technology with live performance\, computational creativity\, and audien
 ce interaction. Participants selected for the labs receive fast-track cons
 ideration for the MOVIDA residencies running in 2027 and 2028.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: MOVIDA (Movement and Virtual Intelligence for the Development and Ac
 cessibility of Artists and Audiences)\nLocation: Four labs across Europe: 
 Bucharest (Romania)\, Dusseldorf (Germany)\, Lisbon and Montemor-o-Novo (P
 ortugal)\, and Tallinn (Estonia). Applications are accepted only from duos
  of one dancer and one creative technologist\; you cannot apply solo. Both
  members must reside in an EU or Creative Europe eligible country\, so Net
 herlands-based applicants qualify.\nAward: EUR 1\,200 gross per artist (EU
 R 2\,400 per duo)\, plus travel and accommodation covered\, plus a product
 ion budget of up to EUR 500 per duo. Accessibility and personal-assistance
  costs are covered by separate agreement. No application fee.\nDuration: N
 ine days per lab\, scheduled between 3 December 2026 and 11 February 2027\
 n\nMore: https://movida.dance/news/call-labs/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://movida.dance/news/call-labs/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Four labs across Europe: Bucharest (Romania)\, Dusseldorf (Germany
 )\, Lisbon and Montemor-o-Novo (Portugal)\, and Tallinn (Estonia). Applica
 tions are accepted only from duos of one dancer and one creative technolog
 ist\; you cannot apply solo. Both members must reside in an EU or Creative
  Europe eligible country\, so Netherlands-based applicants qualify.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art-explora-cite-internationale-des-arts-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260830T103612Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Deadline: Art Explora x Cite internationale des arts Residency Prog
 ramme\, 2027 Sessions
DESCRIPTION:Residency programme run by the Art Explora Foundation with the 
 Cite internationale des arts at its Montmartre site\, supporting work that
  engages scientific and technological exploration and the major social and
  environmental issues of the present. Residents receive a studio-apartment
  of around 50 sqm\, a monthly living grant of EUR 1\,000\, a production gr
 ant of up to EUR 3\,000\, and a round-trip travel grant\, plus access to p
 roduction facilities and local networks. Two tracks are offered: a SOLO pr
 ogramme for artists and writers across visual arts\, performance\, digital
  practices\, literary and other experimental disciplines\, and a COLLECTIV
 E programme for duos or collectives working collaboratively on interdiscip
 linary\, experimental or research-based projects\, for which a single stud
 io-apartment designed for collaborative work hosts two residents sharing a
  bed\, and only one member should submit the application. Eligible artisti
 c disciplines are visual arts\, performance and live arts\, digital arts\,
  curatorial practices\, and writing and literary practices\; eligible rese
 arch fields are humanities\, social sciences\, cultural studies and histor
 y\, technological innovation\, and ecology. No output is required at the e
 nd of the residency\, but participation in the Open Studios is mandatory. 
 ELIGIBILITY: artists\, artist collectives\, researchers\, curators and wri
 ters of all nationalities\, no age restriction\, with a minimum of five ye
 ars of professional activity and works or research exhibited at national o
 r international level. The Cite lists 20 to 22 residencies per year on thi
 s programme. Deadline 6 November 2026\, 23:59 Europe/Paris. Questions: res
 idences@artexplora.org. FLAG: the grant figures above come from the open-c
 all text supplied to the desk\; neither the Cite nor Art Explora publishes
  amounts on the programme page\, so confirm them\, along with the exact de
 adline\, before applying.\n\nOrganisation: Art Explora Foundation with the
  Cite internationale des arts\nLocation: Paris\, France (Cite internationa
 le des arts\, Montmartre site\, 24 rue Norvins\, 75018). Open to applicant
 s of all nationalities with no age restriction.\nAward: Monthly living gra
 nt of EUR 1\,000\, production grant of up to EUR 3\,000\, a round-trip tra
 vel grant\, and a fully equipped studio-apartment of roughly 50 sqm. For c
 ollectives and duos the living grant (up to EUR 2\,000) and the production
  grant (up to EUR 3\,000) are shared between members. Access to production
  facilities and local networks. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 to 6 mont
 hs. Session 1: March to August 2027. Session 2: September 2027 to February
  2028.\n\nMore: https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/en/programme-de-r
 esidence/art-explora-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/en/programme-de-residence/art-
 explora-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Cite internationale des arts\, Montmartre site\, 2
 4 rue Norvins\, 75018). Open to applicants of all nationalities with no ag
 e restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T103612Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
